    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d739">

                <pb facs="0706" n="694" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg694"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.5041/7: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hibbard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-02-01T19:00:00-04:00">February 1, 1943—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>17. Your 12, January 27, 6 a.m. Department has been informed by Firestone that
                    labor bill was passed by Legislature January 29. However, the President
                    intimated on his return from Africa<anchor n="36" xml:id="d739-f1"/> that the
                    subject had been broached to President Barclay and a solution reached. Please
                    report any information you may have.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d739-f1" n="36" xml:id="d739-f1-content">
                <p>For a report on President Roosevelt’s visit to Liberia, see <ref target="#pg658"
                        >p. 658</ref>.</p>
            </note>
